    skos:altLabel 'Tz'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Zero-crossing period'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A wave statistic parameter. Wave period is the time between two successive designated events in the waveform. Zero-crossing is an event where the waveform crosses the zero axis formed by the record average level in a given direction. Normally this crossing is from negative to positive known as an up-crossing.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:S06::S0600108'^^xsd:string .
